Part 3 gitignore correctness for submission

current .gitignore:
data/
logs/
*.csv
*.latencies
benchmark/results/**
reports/handoff/
*.zip

problem:
*.csv and benchmark/results/** currently ignore result CSVs that a notebook may need. benchmark/results/offline_de remains ignored, including latency.csv and summary.csv files generated there.

proposed scheme:
keep raw and intermediate output ignored, but reserve benchmark/results/final/ for small curated submission data.

suggested rules:
*.csv
benchmark/results/**
!benchmark/results/final/
!benchmark/results/final/**
!benchmark/results/final/**/*.csv
!benchmark/results/final/**/*.json
!benchmark/results/final/**/*.md
benchmark/results/final/**/*.latencies
benchmark/results/final/**/*.bin

usage:
put only notebook-facing summary CSVs and small metadata under benchmark/results/final/. Leave raw per-message latency binaries, .latencies, and large sweep trees ignored. Keep root summary.csv ignored unless it is deliberately moved or regenerated into benchmark/results/final/.

size of proposed tracked result files now:
benchmark/results/final is ABSENT, so proposed tracked bytes now: 0.
root summary.csv exists and is ignored; size is 95795 bytes. If promoted to benchmark/results/final/summary.csv, proposed tracked CSV bytes would be 95795, but no file was moved in this pass.

tracked files under reports/handoff:
reports/handoff/stage_7.md: title '# Stage 7 Rate Sweep'. Looks like a previous sweep report. Potentially useful background, but may confuse if superseded by corrected report.
reports/handoff/stage_7_baseline.md: title '# Stage 7 Baseline'. Looks like baseline report. Appropriate if clearly labeled as baseline.
reports/handoff/stage_7_corrected.md: title '# Stage 7 Corrected Rate Sweep'. Looks like corrected/superseding sweep report. Most appropriate of the three for a grader if Stage 7 is still relevant.

recommendation:
Do not rely on ignored benchmark/results/offline_de for submission. Create a curated benchmark/results/final/ tree in a later pass and update .gitignore with the exceptions above.
